WEBVTT

00:00:08.330 --> 00:00:11.680
All right!

00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:14.670
Huh? What?

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:15.780
Gion-kun?

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:17.610
Wh-What are you doing?

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:20.660
Try!

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:22.100
Ow...

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:25.040
Please stop, Gion-kun.

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:32.180
I did it. I pulled off an Ultra Super Try...

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:34.460
Twenty points in one play.

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:40.060
There's no such try, Gion-kun.

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:53.450
I can't believe that didn't wake them up.

00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:01.490
What's wrong?

00:01:02.330 --> 00:01:03.300
Are you okay?

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:06.300
I'm just going to the bathroom.

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:17.880
Is that Ebumi-senpai?

00:01:28.310 --> 00:01:31.210
Where's he going dressed like that?

00:03:21.990 --> 00:03:26.990
<b>Episode 6
Giving Everything You've Got</b>

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:28.410
Where are you going?

00:03:29.410 --> 00:03:33.210
Yesterday, you left while it was 
still dark out and came back late.

00:03:33.740 --> 00:03:37.100
I thought you were going to 
take it easy in your retirement.

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:38.740
I've got work.

00:03:38.740 --> 00:03:39.320
What?

00:03:41.210 --> 00:03:44.820
I'm going to put some kids
through the wringer.

00:03:46.590 --> 00:03:50.830
I dreamed that we made a spectacular 
comeback because I scored this crazy try,

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:53.430
thanks to some secret training
I'd been doing.

00:03:53.430 --> 00:03:55.700
Yeah, yeah. Good for you.

00:03:55.700 --> 00:03:58.410
Maybe I really will get to do 
some secret training...

00:03:58.410 --> 00:04:01.180
What do you think, Tree Trunk?

00:04:01.180 --> 00:04:02.470
Tch.

00:04:02.470 --> 00:04:05.620
You've already told everyone about it,
so I don't think it'd be very secret.

00:04:05.620 --> 00:04:06.900
Oh, right!

00:04:07.910 --> 00:04:10.900
I wish I could be as optimistic 
as the first-years.

00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:15.560
Some guys in my class are going 
to Hawaii during Golden Week.

00:04:15.560 --> 00:04:17.610
Unbelievable.

00:04:17.610 --> 00:04:19.390
What club are they in?

00:04:19.390 --> 00:04:22.170
I don't know. Probably on the soccer team.

00:04:22.170 --> 00:04:26.620
By contrast, we're here 
training during Golden Week.

00:04:26.620 --> 00:04:28.540
In this sausage fest.

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:33.370
If you'd rather go on vacation or dates,
you can leave right now.

00:04:35.890 --> 00:04:36.810
Gather round.

00:04:40.270 --> 00:04:42.400
It's only the second day 
of the training camp.

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:43.590
Don't drag your feet.

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:46.330
You're already warmed up, right?

00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:48.560
Go do ten laps around the school.

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:49.520
What?

00:04:49.520 --> 00:04:50.620
All right!

00:04:53.890 --> 00:04:55.950
Is he stupid?

00:04:55.950 --> 00:04:57.240
Get going already.

00:04:57.240 --> 00:04:58.360
Y-Yes, sir!

00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:12.370
Backs, you'll practice attacking the line.

00:05:13.210 --> 00:05:14.790
Up the accuracy of your passes.

00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:15.710
All right.

00:05:15.710 --> 00:05:19.500
A team of small guys like yours 
needs to do this to win.

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:20.650
Skip one.

00:05:25.960 --> 00:05:27.590
You almost dropped that one!

00:05:48.030 --> 00:05:49.240
Sorry.

00:05:51.610 --> 00:05:53.430
That wasn't a knock-on.

00:05:53.430 --> 00:05:54.240
What?

00:05:54.900 --> 00:05:58.170
It bounced backwards. 
The ball's still in play!

00:05:58.170 --> 00:06:00.420
Why are you <i>walking</i> to the ball?!

00:06:11.450 --> 00:06:13.630
I'll be more careful next time.

00:06:16.250 --> 00:06:18.190
Okay, here it comes.

00:06:19.160 --> 00:06:19.710
Here.

00:06:23.070 --> 00:06:25.410
Hey, you caught it.

00:06:25.410 --> 00:06:27.940
Try relaxing a little more next time.

00:06:27.940 --> 00:06:28.740
Yes, sir!

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:31.070
Don't mess with me!

00:06:37.990 --> 00:06:39.870
How many times do I have to tell you?!

00:06:39.870 --> 00:06:43.130
If you're not up for this, go watch
from the sidelines, you useless piss stain!

00:06:47.210 --> 00:06:48.420
Ebumi again, huh?

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:53.180
What's your problem?

00:06:53.180 --> 00:06:55.080
Who do you think you are?!

00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:57.400
Don't tell me what to do
after skipping all those sessions!

00:07:00.100 --> 00:07:04.420
I-I've never skipped a practice session.
I'm way better than—

00:07:04.420 --> 00:07:10.010
It's because I don't want to waste my time
practicing with nonchalant idiots like you!

00:07:10.010 --> 00:07:12.270
It'll make me worse!

00:07:13.970 --> 00:07:16.030
Hey, that's enough.

00:07:21.490 --> 00:07:24.380
Then go join the track team
or something, Ebumi.

00:07:26.220 --> 00:07:27.460
What?

00:07:27.460 --> 00:07:29.550
Look at how many guys we have.

00:07:29.550 --> 00:07:31.610
Of course we have a range of abilities here.

00:07:32.350 --> 00:07:34.390
Guys who can't work in a team

00:07:34.890 --> 00:07:37.640
slow us down a hundred times more.
Realize that.

00:07:41.660 --> 00:07:44.600
You went somewhere yesterday.

00:07:44.600 --> 00:07:46.890
I saw you go.

00:07:48.190 --> 00:07:53.460
What's wrong? Did you sneak out to 
find some nighttime entertainment?

00:07:53.950 --> 00:07:56.400
Suwa, you asshole!

00:07:56.400 --> 00:07:58.520
How long are you going to keep fighting?

00:08:00.910 --> 00:08:03.580
Backs, go cool your heads.

00:08:05.100 --> 00:08:06.420
Ten laps around the school.

00:08:11.450 --> 00:08:12.860
Get going already.

00:08:20.420 --> 00:08:21.820
What's his problem?

00:08:22.940 --> 00:08:26.930
He really should just quit already.

00:08:29.930 --> 00:08:31.550
That's all for today.

00:08:33.690 --> 00:08:35.200
Put the equipment away.

00:08:47.100 --> 00:08:47.980
Captain.

00:08:49.130 --> 00:08:50.690
Captain Sekizan.

00:08:50.690 --> 00:08:51.450
Yes, sir.

00:08:55.610 --> 00:08:58.220
Captain, you...

00:08:58.220 --> 00:09:00.350
No, all of you...

00:09:01.810 --> 00:09:04.350
What has your goal been up to now?

00:09:10.960 --> 00:09:12.650
W-Well...

00:09:12.650 --> 00:09:15.610
You can't answer that immediately?

00:09:15.610 --> 00:09:19.120
I-It's Hanazono.

00:09:21.490 --> 00:09:22.360
Hey...

00:09:24.260 --> 00:09:26.000
What's Hanazono?

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:28.740
You idiot, Gion! Can't you 
feel the mood right now?

00:09:28.740 --> 00:09:30.960
You don't even know that?

00:09:30.960 --> 00:09:33.180
What? But...

00:09:33.180 --> 00:09:37.330
Hanazono is the rugby 
equivalent of Koshien.

00:09:37.330 --> 00:09:40.170
It's where the national high school 
rugby tournament takes place.

00:09:40.170 --> 00:09:41.760
Oh, wow!

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:44.680
Such a thing exists? I want to go!

00:09:44.680 --> 00:09:46.480
Easier said than done.

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:48.820
Everyone wants to go, but...

00:09:48.820 --> 00:09:50.770
You'll never make it.

00:09:54.500 --> 00:09:57.400
All you have is this worn-out equipment.

00:09:57.950 --> 00:10:02.910
And you start looking reproachful 
when practice gets a little tough.

00:10:04.410 --> 00:10:05.410
How could you ever make it?

00:10:15.040 --> 00:10:16.110
Don't make light of it.

00:10:17.120 --> 00:10:18.670
Go clean yourselves up.

00:10:20.900 --> 00:10:21.680
Hey.

00:10:21.680 --> 00:10:23.830
What do we need to do to go, then?

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:28.690
I want to go to Hanazono!

00:10:32.790 --> 00:10:39.210
If you really want to go,
then practice will get tens of times harder.

00:10:42.190 --> 00:10:43.780
Fine by me! Let's go!

00:11:00.930 --> 00:11:03.930
<b>Welcome 
home</b>

00:11:00.930 --> 00:11:03.930
<b>Did you put 
them through 
the wringer 
today?</b>

00:11:01.740 --> 00:11:03.930
<b>Yeah</b>

00:11:02.240 --> 00:11:03.930
<b>Some of 
them 
almost 
cried</b>

00:11:02.740 --> 00:11:03.930
<b>Oh, my</b>

00:11:04.120 --> 00:11:06.930
<b>Hey, Oharano</b>

00:11:04.600 --> 00:11:06.930
<b>You going to 
bed already?</b>

00:11:05.370 --> 00:11:06.930
<b>He's still upset
 we threw him 
in the scrum.</b>

00:12:01.540 --> 00:12:03.820
What are you doing here, Matsu-san?

00:12:05.180 --> 00:12:07.330
Are you really going to join the track team?

00:12:11.820 --> 00:12:14.860
What? No way.

00:12:18.990 --> 00:12:22.430
Matsu-san, if you're free right now, 
could you ride on this thing?

00:12:22.430 --> 00:12:23.340
What?

00:12:25.430 --> 00:12:27.850
I'm pretty heavy.

00:13:13.120 --> 00:13:15.890
I've never seen you so tired before.

00:13:21.570 --> 00:13:23.610
You've got stamina.

00:13:23.610 --> 00:13:27.100
The night runs didn't start 
last night, did they?

00:13:31.450 --> 00:13:33.120
Not very upfront, are you?

00:13:34.100 --> 00:13:37.370
You're taking this more 
seriously than anyone else.

00:13:41.530 --> 00:13:43.510
I'm not.

00:13:45.180 --> 00:13:47.880
I just want to win.

00:13:50.380 --> 00:13:54.520
I've always been someone 
who gets into lots of fights.

00:13:54.520 --> 00:13:57.190
Who the hell are you? Cheeky, aren't ya?

00:13:57.190 --> 00:14:01.130
Is that how you treat your seniors? 
You pickin' a fight with us?

00:14:01.130 --> 00:14:03.000
Let us teach you a lesson.

00:14:03.000 --> 00:14:06.650
You've got to respect
the pecking order here at Jinko—

00:14:12.390 --> 00:14:15.750
I'd never been in a club before.

00:14:16.330 --> 00:14:19.150
I wasn't expecting that
to change in high school.

00:14:20.710 --> 00:14:22.400
But then...

00:14:24.890 --> 00:14:27.630
<b>Rugby 
Team</b>

00:14:24.890 --> 00:14:27.630
Hey, guys. Wanna play rugby?

00:14:28.330 --> 00:14:32.140
Mutsumi-san reached out to me.

00:14:42.520 --> 00:14:44.480
Go! Go!

00:15:00.750 --> 00:15:02.750
Yeah!

00:15:04.520 --> 00:15:07.510
I couldn't believe this sport existed.

00:15:10.360 --> 00:15:15.380
That's when I remembered a line
I heard on a TV show a long time ago...

00:15:16.380 --> 00:15:19.390
"Rugby is just lawful brawling."

00:15:19.940 --> 00:15:22.610
The rules allow you to 
wipe out your opponent.

00:15:22.610 --> 00:15:26.200
The stupid junk I'd been doing was a sport!

00:15:31.200 --> 00:15:33.910
And what man wants to lose a fight?

00:15:35.660 --> 00:15:38.890
I hated last year's third-years.

00:15:38.890 --> 00:15:41.540
They smiled even when they lost.

00:15:41.540 --> 00:15:45.170
And that attitude still lingers
in our current backs.

00:15:48.240 --> 00:15:53.300
The third-years during our first year
were guys who smiled when they lost, too.

00:15:54.820 --> 00:15:59.850
But, honestly, I don't really remember them.

00:16:03.250 --> 00:16:06.440
Because I couldn't take my eyes off Taku,

00:16:07.140 --> 00:16:10.370
who was the only one caked in mud
and shedding bitter tears when we lost.

00:16:20.420 --> 00:16:24.150
Earlier, when I saw you practicing,
drenched in sweat,

00:16:24.150 --> 00:16:26.460
it reminded me of how Taku was back then.

00:16:29.690 --> 00:16:32.470
It makes me feel pathetic.

00:16:32.780 --> 00:16:36.550
You are pathetic!
You let Oharano take your position!

00:16:38.410 --> 00:16:44.330
But, until last year, our team would've 
called an experienced first-year "insolent"

00:16:44.330 --> 00:16:46.650
and refused to let him play in any matches.

00:16:49.020 --> 00:16:50.840
The team is changing.

00:16:51.770 --> 00:16:54.240
I need to change with it.

00:16:58.370 --> 00:17:00.260
I'm glad I got to talk to you.

00:17:01.300 --> 00:17:04.570
If you're going to run tomorrow, 
do you mind if I join you?

00:17:04.570 --> 00:17:07.680
Jeez, you really are pathetic.

00:17:07.680 --> 00:17:09.790
Do whatever you want.

00:17:11.380 --> 00:17:14.380
What?! You beat me to it!

00:17:15.430 --> 00:17:18.530
That's not fair,
Matsu-senpai and Truant Delinquent!

00:17:18.530 --> 00:17:20.130
I'll kill you, you little turd.

00:17:20.130 --> 00:17:23.080
I came out here to train in secret, too!

00:17:23.080 --> 00:17:24.780
Gion, keep it down.

00:17:35.190 --> 00:17:37.610
Ebumi, you've been practicing on your own?

00:17:37.610 --> 00:17:39.070
Let us join you.

00:17:50.970 --> 00:17:53.960
I thought you'd gone home.

00:17:57.770 --> 00:17:59.970
Who the hell would? Screw off.

00:18:03.880 --> 00:18:06.450
Disrupt the harmony of the team again,
and I'll kick you out.

00:18:06.450 --> 00:18:08.310
Shut up. Go die.

00:18:09.230 --> 00:18:11.750
Let's play some touch football!

00:18:11.750 --> 00:18:13.530
Yeah!

00:18:13.530 --> 00:18:15.240
Guys...

00:18:22.940 --> 00:18:24.650
Go to sleep!

00:18:30.660 --> 00:18:32.670
Two hours of running passes starting now.

00:18:34.430 --> 00:18:36.850
Running for two hours straight?

00:18:36.850 --> 00:18:38.810
Didn't you say you were going to Hanazono?

00:18:38.810 --> 00:18:41.000
Then, steel yourselves.

00:18:41.000 --> 00:18:43.050
Yeah! Let's get on with it!

00:19:05.210 --> 00:19:08.370
You're not taking this seriously,
thinking "it's just practice," aren't you?

00:19:09.450 --> 00:19:13.270
If this were a game,
your opponents would now have the ball.

00:19:44.220 --> 00:19:46.450
I can't... keep going...

00:19:47.460 --> 00:19:48.580
I'm dying...

00:19:51.500 --> 00:19:53.850
If you have the energy to complain, run!

00:19:54.760 --> 00:19:59.260
Even in our current state,
we can still give everything we've got!

00:20:03.600 --> 00:20:06.350
Dammit!

00:20:06.770 --> 00:20:08.850
I want to go to Koshien!

00:20:08.850 --> 00:20:10.630
It's Hanazono, you idiot!

00:20:08.850 --> 00:20:11.350
<b>Hanazono</b>

00:20:10.370 --> 00:20:11.350
Jump

00:20:11.770 --> 00:20:14.150
O-Of course we want to go!

00:20:14.150 --> 00:20:20.150
But when guys like us say it,
 it just sounds lame.

00:20:20.150 --> 00:20:21.690
What's lame about it?

00:20:49.140 --> 00:20:51.600
Okay, that's enough.

00:20:57.330 --> 00:20:58.610
I'm dying...

00:21:02.430 --> 00:21:05.630
Do you know what it means to go "all out"?

00:21:07.120 --> 00:21:10.790
It's what your captain said earlier.

00:21:14.270 --> 00:21:16.370
"Give everything you've got."

00:21:17.120 --> 00:21:19.880
You don't have the strength or
 technical skills you need to win.

00:21:20.430 --> 00:21:24.880
But if you're prepared to 
go all out, day in, day out...

00:21:25.740 --> 00:21:28.340
If your determination to do that
is the strongest in Japan,

00:21:28.810 --> 00:21:32.390
you might even make it to Hanazono.

00:21:42.840 --> 00:21:44.860
<i>I don't have children,</i>

00:21:46.810 --> 00:21:48.910
<i>so there are things I don't know.</i>

00:21:50.600 --> 00:21:55.600
<i>They have even less of a way with words
than I'd realized.</i>

00:21:59.130 --> 00:22:02.920
<i>This job might be harder than I thought.</i>

00:22:03.930 --> 00:22:05.970
I want to go to Hanazono!

00:22:05.970 --> 00:22:08.180
Some of you still have energy.

00:22:08.180 --> 00:22:10.040
Let's keep running for another hour.

00:22:10.040 --> 00:22:11.290
Gion, you idiot!

00:22:11.290 --> 00:22:13.460
Keep your mouth shut!

00:23:44.940 --> 00:23:49.940
<b>Next Time: "I Want to Be Able to Do Everything"</b>

00:23:45.940 --> 00:23:49.170
Next time: "I Want to Be 
Able to Do Everything."
